latest_plan = "Based on the reflection, here's a detailed step-by-step plan to solve the challenge:\n\n1. Analyze the Input Grid:\n   a. Identify all non-blue color clusters.\n   b. For each cluster, determine its size, shape, and available space around it.\n\n2. Prioritize Clusters:\n   a. Sort clusters by size in descending order.\n   b. Create a queue of clusters to process.\n\n3. For Each Cluster:\n   a. Determine Expansion Strategy:\n      - If the cluster is compact (e.g., 2x2 or smaller), plan for outward expansion.\n      - If the cluster is spread out or has a distinct shape, plan to fill in and slightly expand.\n   \n   b. Calculate Target Size:\n      - For small clusters (1-3 cells), aim for 4-6 cells.\n      - For medium clusters (4-8 cells), aim for 8-12 cells.\n      - For large clusters (9+ cells), cap at 16 cells or 1.5 times original size, whichever is smaller.\n\n   c. Create Expansion Queue:\n      - Identify all adjacent empty (blue) cells.\n      - Prioritize cells that maintain or enhance the cluster's shape.\n      - For fill-in expansions, prioritize internal empty cells.\n\n   d. Expand the Cluster:\n      - While the cluster size is less than the target and there are available cells:\n        * Select the highest priority cell from the expansion queue.\n        * Change the cell to the cluster's color.\n        * Update the cluster size and shape.\n        * Recalculate priorities for remaining cells in the expansion queue.\n\n   e. Shape Refinement:\n      - Fill in single-cell gaps within the expanded shape.\n      - Remove isolated cells not connected to the main body.\n\n4. Conflict Resolution:\n   - If expansion of one cluster interferes with another:\n     a. Reduce the target size of the conflicting clusters.\n     b. Attempt to expand in non-conflicting directions.\n     c. If conflict persists, prioritize the larger or more established cluster.\n\n5. Global Refinement:\n   a. Scan the entire grid for any remaining single-cell islands of color.\n   b. Either connect these to nearby clusters of the same color or revert to blue.\n\n6. Final Pass:\n   - Make a final pass over the grid to ensure all expansions are coherent and meet the size and shape criteria.\n\n7. Validation:\n   - Check that each original cluster has been expanded appropriately.\n   - Verify that no unintended color mixing has occurred.\n   - Ensure the overall distribution and balance of colors is maintained.\n\nImplementation Notes:\n- Use a priority queue for managing expansion cells, with priorities based on how well they fit the desired shape and fill strategy.\n- Implement a flood-fill algorithm for identifying and expanding clusters.\n- Use a grid-based distance calculation to maintain the general position and shape of clusters during expansion.\n- Employ a sliding window approach for shape analysis to determine the best expansion strategy for each cluster.\n\nThis plan is flexible enough to handle various initial configurations while still providing a structured approach to expanding and refining color clusters. It addresses the observed patterns in all examples and should be able to handle edge cases and conflicts between expanding clusters."
